<title>HUNGARY: CENTRAL EUROPE'S CESI HITS NEW HIGH.</title>
<headline>CENTRAL EUROPE'S CESI HITS NEW HIGH.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index rose on Thursday to a new high of 1,519.44 points, up 11.79 points or 0.78 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index gained mainly due to rises on the Czech and the Hungarian market.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.	   -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
